        <mxCell id="hfrgqyCwfU7HqbW_KAcQ-26" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;strokeColor=none;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Bilateral time-weighted RULA (mean and asymmetry) was merged with the prespecified demographic, physiological, and work-organisation predictors, and with a separate three-class outcome (Low/Medium/High) derived from the tertile-thresholded MSD Index. Names, participant identifiers, the MSD Index, the Risk Class label, and the nine pain indicators were excluded from the predictor matrix.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
